WEBVTT

1
00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:14.409
When Vinnie and Mandy finished the Iroquois trip, Dad had opened the attic door suddenly.

2
00:00:14.410 --> 00:00:18.008
Then he slipped and twisted his ankle.

3
00:00:18.009 --> 00:00:22.762
"Oh, that hurts!" Dad said in pain.

4
00:00:22.763 --> 00:00:26.670
He was sitting in his favorite chair in the living room.

5
00:00:26.671 --> 00:00:30.556
Mom held a bag of ice on his swollen foot.

6
00:00:30.557 --> 00:00:36.551
"I was going to clean up the attic, but I can't now," Dad said.

7
00:00:36.552 --> 00:00:38.971
"Can you kids do it?"

8
00:00:38.972 --> 00:00:43.150
Vinnie and Mandy clapped their hands excitedly.

9
00:00:43.151 --> 00:00:49.638
"Sure, we'll take care of it," said Vinnie cheerfully.

10
00:00:49.639 --> 00:00:52.034
"What's so special about that attic?"

11
00:00:52.035 --> 00:00:55.345
Dad asked Mom as the kids ran off.

12
00:00:55.346 --> 00:00:59.554
The children raced up the attic stairs.

13
00:00:59.555 --> 00:01:03.742
Mandy grabbed the photo album.

14
00:01:03.743 --> 00:01:08.014
"Let's guess where we're going next," she said.

15
00:01:08.015 --> 00:01:13.670
"Okay, I'm going to guess Africa!" said Vinnie.

16
00:01:13.671 --> 00:01:16.708
"I think it's going to be China!"

17
00:01:16.709 --> 00:01:20.684
said Mandy, opening the photo album.

18
00:01:20.685 --> 00:01:23.001
They were both wrong.

19
00:01:23.002 --> 00:01:28.779
In the photo, the old man was standing in front of a large tower.

20
00:01:28.780 --> 00:01:33.087
There were big black birds flying around his head.

21
00:01:33.088 --> 00:01:37.064
A group of men with spears were marching together.

22
00:01:37.065 --> 00:01:42.076
The spears were glowing.

23
00:01:42.077 --> 00:01:46.880
"Where is this?" asked Vinnie.

24
00:01:46.881 --> 00:01:50.808
"It looks like . . ." began Mandy.

25
00:01:50.809 --> 00:01:54.274
The light forced them to close their eyes.

26
00:01:54.275 --> 00:02:01.884
The children fell down the dark tunnel.

27
00:02:01.885 --> 00:02:03.860
Mandy landed first.

28
00:02:03.861 --> 00:02:05.669
She opened her eyes.

29
00:02:05.670 --> 00:02:10.756
Two horses pulling a wagon were coming straight at her.

30
00:02:10.757 --> 00:02:16.426
Screaming, Mandy jumped out of the way.

31
00:02:16.427 --> 00:02:21.754
Then she tripped, fell, and scraped her knee badly.

32
00:02:21.755 --> 00:02:27.569
"Whoa!" The driver of the wagon stopped the horses.

33
00:02:27.570 --> 00:02:29.815
"Where did you come from, miss?

34
00:02:29.816 --> 00:02:32.878
I didn't see anyone walking in the street."

35
00:02:32.879 --> 00:02:35.867
The driver scratched his head.

36
00:02:35.868 --> 00:02:41.880
"I . . . I'm terribly sorry, sir," Mandy stammered.

37
00:02:41.881 --> 00:02:44.137
Her legs felt shaky.

38
00:02:44.138 --> 00:02:47.493
"Where am I?" she wondered.

39
00:02:47.494 --> 00:02:51.014
"And where is Vinnie?"

40
00:02:51.015 --> 00:02:54.167
Vinnie landed on the same street.

41
00:02:54.168 --> 00:02:56.671
A carriage came toward him.

42
00:02:56.672 --> 00:02:59.271
Vinnie quickly stepped aside.

43
00:02:59.272 --> 00:03:02.887
Looking around, he did not see Mandy.

44
00:03:02.888 --> 00:03:08.352
She was hidden by all the wagons and horses in the street.

45
00:03:08.353 --> 00:03:13.150
"To be or not to be!" cried a voice.

46
00:03:13.151 --> 00:03:16.802
Vinnie saw a boy behind some barrels.

47
00:03:16.803 --> 00:03:19.874
He was reading from a piece of paper.

48
00:03:19.875 --> 00:03:22.617
The boy did not see Vinnie.

49
00:03:22.618 --> 00:03:27.161
"That is the question!" continued the boy.

50
00:03:27.162 --> 00:03:32.134
"Ahem," said Vinnie, clearing his throat.

51
00:03:32.135 --> 00:03:35.216
"Hey, stop spying on me!"

52
00:03:35.217 --> 00:03:38.080
said the boy, hiding the paper.

53
00:03:38.081 --> 00:03:40.347
"Who are you?"

54
00:03:40.348 --> 00:03:42.261
"My name is Vinnie.

55
00:03:42.262 --> 00:03:45.811
Who are you, and what are you reading?"

56
00:03:45.812 --> 00:03:47.966
"My name is Edward,"

57
00:03:47.967 --> 00:03:51.200
said the boy, bowing dramatically.

58
00:03:51.201 --> 00:03:55.072
"I am reading a play by Shakespeare!"

59
00:03:55.073 --> 00:03:58.491
The name sounded familiar to Vinnie.

60
00:03:58.492 --> 00:04:04.204
"Someday, I will be England's greatest actor!" shouted Edward.

61
00:04:04.205 --> 00:04:10.926
"Someday, I will perform before the queen!"
